# Web Hooks

Prefer project-local tooling and do not wire hooks to remote one-off package
execution.

If hooks are introduced in a later phase:

1. Format or lint the changed file with the repository-owned Biome command.
2. Run the narrow affected Nx target only when its latency is suitable for a
   hook.
3. Keep builds, Jest, Playwright, and global checks explicit; do not run them
   automatically after every edit or at every session stop.

Never use a hook to install packages, invoke alternate project tooling, deploy
services, or inspect `ui_demo.json`. This rule does not authorize creating hook
configuration.
